```
1. item

para
.
<ol>
<li>
item
</li>
</ol>
<p>para</p>
```

Only single letter alphabetic list markers.

```
word. Continuing paragraph.
.
<p>word. Continuing paragraph.</p>
```

Prioritize current type when ambigiuous.

```
A) first
B) second
C) third
D) fourth
E) fifth
.
<ol type="A">
<li>
first
</li>
<li>
second
</li>
<li>
third
</li>
<li>
fourth
</li>
<li>
fifth
</li>
</ol>
```

Numbered lists can use roman numerals

```
mdclxvi) 1666
mdclxvii) 1667
MDCLXVIII) 1668
MDCLXVIX) 1669
.
<ol start="1666" type="i">
<li>
1666
</li>
<li>
1667
</li>
</ol>
<ol start="1668" type="I">
<li>
1668
</li>
<li>
1669
</li>
</ol>
```

An ordered list with a style change should be split in two

```
i. a
j) d
.
<ol type="i">
<li>
a
</li>
</ol>
<ol start="10" type="a">
<li>
d
</li>
</ol>
```

```
- - - a
   {0=0}
   {0=0}
   b
.
<ul>
<li>
<ul>
<li>
<ul>
<li>
a
</li>
</ul>
b
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
```

```
-
 {}
 {}
 a
.
<ul>
<li>
a
</li>
</ul>
```

List should break if an item is incompatible with the start item even if it is
compatible with the previous item.

```
DD)
D)
E)
.
<ol start="1000" type="I">
<li>
</li>
<li>
</li>
</ol>
<ol start="5" type="A">
<li>
</li>
</ol>
```

